Z||000000||Fiero_24||07-07-2001||09:41 PM||||The engine heats up really fast, and while driving I always have to turn on the cooling fan for the radiator (I added a switch since my air still works).  Take a 10 mile drive and the engine is really hot.  You can stick your hand in there and just feel the heat coming off.  Could this be the water pump going bad?  I do not see any antifreeze leaking out of the hole on the bottom.  I did make sure the system was "burped" correctly, and I am going to try a new thermostat tomorrow.  The other thing is that you can notice on acceleration from a stop sign that you feel very small  (almost like a spark plug misfire) hessitations.  This is on an 87GT.  Could the 2 be related in any way.  I am not sure if I am explaining this correctly.<P>Craig<P><BR>------------------<BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero_24</A> <BR>1987 GT<p>[This message has been edited by Fiero_24 (edited 07-09-2001).]||||reg||5
